  "description": "<p>I have installed fcrepo4-oaiprovider-4.2.0 on Fedora 4.2.0 (plus-rbacl-audit). I have added sets using command below.<br/>\ncurl -X POST <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/fcrepo-webapp-plus-rbacl-audit-4.2.0/rest/oai/sets\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/fcrepo-webapp-plus-rbacl-audit-4.2.0/rest/oai/sets</a> -H \"Content-Type: text/xml\" -d @oai_set.xml -u fedoraAdmin:fedoraAdmin </p>\n\n<p>Here is my @oai_set.xml<br/>\n&lt;?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\" standalone=\"yes\"?&gt;<br/>\n  &lt;set xmlns:ns2=\"http://www.openarchives.org/OAI/2.0/\"&gt;<br/>\n    &lt;ns2:setSpec&gt;oai-test-set&lt;/ns2:setSpec&gt;<br/>\n    &lt;ns2:setName&gt;oai-test-set&lt;/ns2:setName&gt;<br/>\n  &lt;/set&gt;</p>\n\n<p>It was working for the first set. I have added another set, oai-test-set-2 and then list the set by using oai?verb=ListSets, but the response showed only first set.</p>\n\n<p>Here are my questions</p>\n<ul class=\"alternate\" type=\"square\">\n\t<li>How can I make the OAI Provider to show all sets?</li>\n\t<li>How can I update or delete oai set?</li>\n</ul>\n",
